# `data/phase1_data.csv` -- the only tracked CSV here -- is written by Python's
# `csv` module, which terminates rows with RFC-4180 CRLF. (The Phase 2 CSVs are
# gitignored and are written by joining on "\n", so they are unaffected either
# way; the pattern below covers them only incidentally.) Two consequences, and
# one attribute each.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion entirely. `data/phase1_data.csv` is
# tracked (it is the exact-value oracle the Phase 2 bound tests run against)
# and its SHA-256 is compared with the one `data/manifest.json` records at
# generation time, by
# tests/test_phase2_bounds.py::test_the_tracked_oracle_matches_its_manifest_provenance.
# A clone under `core.autocrlf` that rewrote CRLF to LF would change those
# bytes and fail that check for a reason with nothing to do with the
# mathematics. Byte-for-byte is the point.
#
# `-whitespace` stops `git diff --check` reporting the CR at the end of every
# row as trailing whitespace. It is the csv module's row terminator, not
# sloppy editing, and these files are generated and never hand-edited.
data/*.csv -text -whitespace
